  "components": [],
  "timeoriginalestimate": null,
  "description": {
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1,
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Description"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Two things about sorting on Sales By Customer are wrong."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The Location column cannot be sorted \u2014 it has no sort arrow and clicking it does nothing, while every other column sorts."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "And rows with no value sort to the wrong end: sorting Margin % smallest-first puts the blank ones at the top, and largest-first puts them at the bottom."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Steps to reproduce"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Environment: QA branch sv8582 (https://sv8582.qa.shopview.com). Desktop browser, signed in as an Admin."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "orderedList",
     "attrs": {
      "order": 1
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Open Reports, then Sales By Customer, and choose This Year so there are plenty of rows \u2014 that view holds 384 customers."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Click each column heading in turn. Every one sorts except Location."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "listItem",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "paragraph",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "text",
           "text": "Click Margin % once, for smallest first, and look at the first rows. Click it again, for largest first, and look again. Here 19 of the first 30 rows had no Margin % value. This was seen with Product Type Parts & Service and both locations selected, Staging Heavy Duty - 9919 and Staging Lethbridge - 4310."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Current behaviour"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Location has no sort arrow and does not respond to a click. The server itself sorts by location correctly when asked, so this is missing from the screen only."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Sorting Margin % smallest-first puts the rows with a dash instead of a percentage at the top; largest-first moves them to the end. That is the opposite way round."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The sorting is genuinely applied and not a stale screen \u2014 each click sends a fresh request, the first page comes back in the new order, and the heading reports which way it is sorted. The order on the other twelve columns is correct."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Expected behaviour"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Location sorts like every other column, apart from the arrow column at the far left. Rows with no value sort to the bottom when sorting smallest-first and to the top when sorting largest-first."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "rule"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Source",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " \u2014 "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "the "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Sales By Customer report specification",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "link",
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://shopview.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020aa00b8d6a71f4259891982a304227c20/pages/577634305/SBC+Sales+By+Customer+Report"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " on Confluence, version 15, requirement S10-R1: \u201cEvery column is sortable except the chevron column.\u201d"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The same description, requirement S10-R3: \u201cA missing value sorts to the bottom in ascending order and to the top in descending order; a Margin % em-dash cell (S7-R12) counts as a missing value.\u201d"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
